# Story 107: Chrome Extension Browser Automation (50s)
# Hook: A rysh pane that lives in your browser's side panel and drives the page.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-107-chrome-extension-browser-automation.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
A rysh pane that lives in your browser's side panel and drives the page.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
The Chrome extension's side panel is a real rysh pane -- same modes, same AI agent -- except its job is to drive the browser you are looking at.

[00:15.0 --> 00:26.0]
It connects to your session the same way every other client does: a NATS-over-WebSocket link back to the bus.

[00:26.0 --> 00:38.0]
Because the agent lives in the pane and not the page, your conversation persists across navigations -- click a link, load a new URL, the agent keeps its full context.

[00:38.0 --> 00:50.0]
Ask the agent to fill a form or pull data, and it acts on the live tab -- a browser copilot wired into your terminal.

